Changes 2024–2026:
*November 2024: Sam Christmas (Liberal Democrats) resigns – by-election held December 2024<ref>{{cite news |last1=Timlin |first1=Josh |title=Resignation prompts council by-election |url=https://www.barnsleychronicle.com/article/30073/resignation-prompts-council-by-election |access-date=16 January 2026 |work=Barnsley Chronicle |date=8 November 2024 |language=en}}</ref>
*December 2024: Andy Waters (Liberal Democrats) wins by-election<ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Dodworth Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/958/#2024-12-12 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=16 January 2026}}</ref>
*July 2025: Clive Pickering (Labour) joins Liberal Democrats<ref>{{cite news |last1=Tolson |first1=Jack |title=Councillor switches his allegiance |url=https://www.barnsleychronicle.com/article/32398/councillor-switches-his-allegiance |access-date=16 January 2026 |work=Barnsley Chronicle |date=4 July 2025 |language=en}}</ref>
*August 2025: Trevor Smith (Labour) leaves party to sit as an independent<ref>{{cite news |last1=Whitehouse |first1=Paul |title=Barnsley politics in confusion with Reform defection claim and counter-claim |url=https://www.rotherhamadvertiser.co.uk/news/politics/barnsley-politics-in-confusion-with-reform-defection-claim-and-counter-claim-5282918 |access-date=16 January 2026 |work=Rotherham Advertiser |date=21 August 2025 |language=en}}</ref>
*December 2025: David White (Independent, previously Reform, elected as Conservative) resigns – seat left vacant until 2026 election<ref>{{cite news |last1=Tolson |first1=Jack |title=Controversial councillor hands in resignation |url=https://www.barnsleychronicle.com/article/34009/controversial-councillor-hands-in-resignation |access-date=16 January 2026 |work=Barnsley Chronicle |date=12 December 2025 |language=en}}</ref>

==Candidates==
288 candidates were validly nominated to contest the 63 seats. The [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour Party]], [[Liberal Democrats (UK)|Liberal Democrats]] and [[Reform UK]] are each fielding a full slate of 63 candidates. The [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservative Party]] and [[Green Party of England and Wales|Green Party]] are fielding 42 candidates each. There are 6 independent candidates, 3 English Democrats, 3 SDP and 3 TUSC.

Liberal Democrat Leader of the Opposition, Hannah Kitching, is not seeking re-election. In addition, six other incumbents are standing down at this election; Alice Cave, Steve Green, Kath Mitchell and Abi Moore of the Labour Party; Steve Hunt of the Liberal Democrats and independent councillor Trevor Smith. Smith had previously been elected as Labour, Democrats and Veterans and Barnsley Independent Group. There was one vacancy at the time of the election, this seat was previously held by independent David White, elected as Conservative, previously Reform UK. All other 55 serving councillors are seeking re-election, with two moving wards.

